Fix sweep-found crashes, pipe deadlocks, injection risks and silent data loss

Second sweep pass (issues #64-#120) over the whole package, each fix verified
with a script against the real francisella_tularensis.db and synthetic xmfa
data; pre-change copies kept in .fix-backups/.

Core fixes:
- DatabaseConnection: multi_update silently failed on every shipped database
  (no UNIQUE constraint on genome) while reporting success; rewritten as
  parameter-bound update-then-insert, ModifyTree now passes value pairs
- update(): SET values parameterized, WHERE bound to a dedicated where value
- get_node(): name bound as a parameter (SQL injection, #67)
- SNPDatabase: shell-free makedirs (#69), missing __version__ import (#119)
- CanSNPer2/runMauve: mauve stdout/stderr redirected straight to the per-run
  log file; the PIPE filled up and hung the poll loop (#68, #85); process
  loop no longer mutates while iterating; cleanup is dir-aware (#86/#87)
- DownloadGenomes: NCBI ftp:// retired in 2021, downloads now use https (#120);
  unzipping done with the gzip module instead of external gunzip (#73/#74)
- NewickTree: invalid newick raises instead of UnboundLocalError (#77),
  missing start node returns a clean rejection (#78), zero-distance guard (#95)
- ModifyTree: malformed modification/name files raise InputError or are
  skipped with warnings instead of IndexError/ValueError (#79-#84, #91-#94)
- P3 hardening across ReadTaxonomy*, ReadCanSNP_tables, ModifyDatabase,
  ParseXMFA, WriteTaxonomy, runMauve, CanSNPerTree: short rows, malformed
  xmfa blocks, empty SNP tables and missing kwargs now fail clearly or skip
  with a warning instead of crashing mid-run (#71-#75, #88-#115)
- Removed leftover one-shot scripts append_issues.py/clean_issues.py that
  could re-corrupt the tracker file (#116/#117)
